==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|French}}, {{m|enm|Frensch}}, {{m|enm|Frensh}}, from {{inh|en|ang|Frencisc||of the [[Frank]]s, Frankish, French}}, from {{m|ang|Franca||a Frank}}. Compare {{cog|goh|Franko||a Frank}}, akin to {{cog|ang|franca||javelin, spear}}, from the use of such weapons by the Franks.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|frĕnch|a=UK,US}}, {{IPA|en|/fɹɛnt͡ʃ/|[fɹ̠ɛn̠t͡ʃ]}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-French.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-french.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Wodencafe-french.wav|a=US}}
