===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To prepare food by [[cut]]ting it into [[strip]]s.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[kiss]] (another person) while [[insert]]ing one’s [[tongue]] into the other person's mouth.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1988|author=Wanda Coleman|title=A War of Eyes and other stories|page=151|passage=Tom '''frenched''' her full in the mouth.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To kiss in this manner.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|author=Susan Steinberg|title=The End of Free Love|page=81|passage=We '''frenched''' by the wall.}}
# {{lb|en|cuisine}} To {{l|en|French trim}}; to stylishly expose bone by removing the fat and meat covering it (as done to a rack of lamb or bone-in rib-eye steak).

